  <video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://globetape.github.io/thumbs/world-today-2026-11-25-h.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>Iowa Lead Azide Detonation: 4,500 kg Destroyed | World News, Nov 25</video:title><video:description>The US Army destroyed about 4,500 kilograms of degraded lead azide at an Iowa ammunition plant, and early EPA readings showed no airborne lead.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://www.youtube.com/embed/CvbJjw6NrsQ</video:player_loc><video:duration>114</video:duration><video:publication_date>2026-11-26T05:21:10Z</video:publication_date><video:family_friendly>yes</video:family_friendly></video:video></url>
<url><loc>https://globetape.github.io/videos/korea-38/</loc><lastmod>2026-11-25</lastmod>
  <image:image><image:loc>https://globetape.github.io/thumbs/korea-38.jpg</image:loc></image:image>
  <video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://globetape.github.io/thumbs/korea-38.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>Did the Korean War Ever Really End?</video:title><video:description>Did the Korean War ever really end? The fighting stopped on 27 July 1953 with an armistice, a military ceasefire, but no peace treaty has ever been signed. And the border it left isn't the 38th parallel: it's where the front line froze.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://www.youtube.com/embed/glrslVz1Xrs</video:player_loc><video:duration>39</video:duration><video:publication_date>2026-11-25T18:00:00Z</video:publication_date><video:family_friendly>yes</video:family_friendly></video:video></url>
<url><loc>https://globetape.github.io/videos/chile-length/</loc><lastmod>2026-11-24</lastmod>
  <image:image><image:loc>https://globetape.github.io/thumbs/chile-length.jpg</image:loc></image:image>
  <video:video><video:thumbnail_loc>https://globetape.github.io/thumbs/chile-length.jpg</video:thumbnail_loc><video:title>Chile Is Longer Than Lisbon to Moscow</video:title><video:description>How long is Chile? 4,270 km from north to south, but only 177 km wide on average. Lay it over Europe with its southern tip on Lisbon and it doesn't stop at Moscow: it keeps going for another 360 km, crossing ten countries on the way.</video:description><video:player_loc>https://www.youtube.com/embed/Rhv_-F-Rd40</video:player_loc><video:duration>40</video:duration><video:publication_date>2026-11-24T18:00:00Z</video:publication_date><video:family_friendly>yes</video:family_friendly></video:video></url>
<url><loc>https://globetape.github.io/videos/world-today-2026-11-23-h/</loc><lastmod>2026-11-24</lastmod>
